      "normalized_sha256": "82fd85d7d877438e349407a829d1e35806842c5943d9c0f294aa58ed3173779c",
      "rationale": "This is the base equation of the recursive derivAcc mathematical summary: processing an empty remaining coefficient sequence returns the accumulator. It defines the named proof term and does not rewrite an execution configuration.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-82fd85d7d877438e349407a829d1e35806842c5943d9c0f294aa58ed3173779c",
      "start_line": 9,
      "text": "  rule derivAcc(ACC:ValSeq, .ValSeq, _I:Int) => ACC [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 13,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "51a3749a6415a476a599f9f4b4d86298466c83cbf2e19efd98a63953ec251c03",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded nonpositive-index recurrence of derivAcc, consuming one sequence constructor while leaving the accumulator unchanged. It is a defining equation for the summary, including its simplification use, rather than an independently asserted mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-51a3749a6415a476a599f9f4b4d86298466c83cbf2e19efd98a63953ec251c03",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule derivAcc(ACC:ValSeq, vCons(_V:Val, REST:ValSeq), I:Int)\n    => derivAcc(ACC, REST, I +Int 1)\n    requires notBool (I >Int 0)\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "699bb53c2b20d45244efa55313af6891bd44df240c352ce9088ca451eccca62c",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded positive-index recurrence of derivAcc, defining the next accumulator by appending the fixed-semantics multiplication term and recursing on the tail. Its left-hand side is the mathematical summary symbol, not a program control term, so the simplification rule is definitional.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-699bb53c2b20d45244efa55313af6891bd44df240c352ce9088ca451eccca62c",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule derivAcc(ACC:ValSeq, vCons(V:Val, REST:ValSeq), I:Int)\n    => derivAcc(\n         valSeqConcat(ACC, vCons(applyBin(\"*\", I, V), .ValSeq)),\n         REST,\n         I +Int 1)\n    requires I >Int 0\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 25,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "69d164c2333b75d39789a2087d0efc8310446075e2ed8ca85aaa99880622898f",
      "rationale": "This equation defines the empty-sequence base case of the total noRefsVS structural predicate. It introduces the meaning of a named input-domain helper and is not an additional theorem about an already defined symbol.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-69d164c2333b75d39789a2087d0efc8310446075e2ed8ca85aaa99880622898f",
      "start_line": 25,
      "text": "  rule noRefsVS(.ValSeq) => true"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 27,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "cdffeaf04d811ef623fa1b34b1412c6bea8d70a043f5ca0aa93d9bec48680e9a",
      "rationale": "This equation recursively defines noRefsVS on a nonempty sequence using the supplied isRefV predicate and the tail. It is the structural step of the named predicate, not an operational observation or a separately trusted domain fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-cdffeaf04d811ef623fa1b34b1412c6bea8d70a043f5ca0aa93d9bec48680e9a",
      "start_line": 26,
      "text": "  rule noRefsVS(vCons(V:Val, REST:ValSeq))\n    => notBool isRefV(V) andBool noRefsVS(REST)"
    }
  ],
